                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c81674bc-de15-3afc-987e-a652c17684ed",
                        "entry_id": "756d2656-0973-3045-bfdd-72647fc7829d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "one who is constantly hungry"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "masculine",
                            "person"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb708be5-6c68-331e-90bd-88fc9aa17dfe",
                        "entry_id": "756d2656-0973-3045-bfdd-72647fc7829d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "one who is suffering from starvation"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine",
                            "obsolete",
                            "person"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e427f6f8-9790-4956-a443-7060bb952851",
                                "sense_id": "fb708be5-6c68-331e-90bd-88fc9aa17dfe",
                                "text": "Oprócz pracowników, zajętych potężną robotą od świtu do nocy na górze trupiej, plątał się tam i wałęsał trzeci jeszcze gatunek istot żywych: — żebraki, głodomory, chorowite kaleki, baby i starcy — słowem, nędza miejska i portowa, ciągnąca za wyżerką przy wojsku.",
                                "translation": "Along with the laborers engaged in back-breaking toil from morning to night on that cadaver-strewn hill, there was also a third category of living beings to be found hanging about: beggars, starvelings, sickly cripples, old men and woman — in a word, the dregs of the city and the port, drawn to the army by the possibility of food.",
                                "english": "Along with the laborers engaged in back-breaking toil from morning to night on that cadaver-strewn hill, there was also a third category of living beings to be found hanging about: beggars, starvelings, sickly cripples, old men and woman — in a word, the dregs of the city and the port, drawn to the army by the possibility of food."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
